Translation patch: `parse_mysql_datetime_string_with_time`

Change: in the branch where `s.len() == 19`, `&s[..19]` becomes `s`.
Why: Aeneas does not model range indexing on `str`.
Behaviour: Identical: `..19` is the whole string when its length is 19 (and the end of a string is a char boundary, so the indexing never panicked).

